# insurance-claims-azure-platform — example environment configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` for local work. `.env` is gitignored; this file is the
# committed schema. Every variable is optional — the default path runs
# fully against Azurite (ADLS emulator) + local PySpark with $0 cost.

# ---------- Azurite (default local path, free) -----------------------
# Spin up with `azurite --silent --location .azurite &` (requires npm +
# node). The storage SDK clients respect the standard dev connection
# string that Azurite publishes in its docs. Copy it from:
#   https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/storage/common/storage-use-azurite#connect-to-azurite-with-sdks-and-tools
# AZURE_STORAGE_CONNECTION_STRING=<see Azurite docs — well-known dev key>
# AZURE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT_NAME=devstoreaccount1
# AZURE_STORAGE_BLOB_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:10000/devstoreaccount1
# AZURE_STORAGE_QUEUE_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:10001/devstoreaccount1
# AZURE_STORAGE_TABLE_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:10002/devstoreaccount1

# ---------- Real Azure (optional, costs real money) ------------------
# Only set these if you want to deploy to a real Azure subscription.
# AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID=...
# AZURE_TENANT_ID=...
# AZURE_CLIENT_ID=...                # Service principal AppId
# AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET=...            # Service principal secret
# AZURE_RESOURCE_GROUP=rg-claims-dev
# AZURE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT=claimsadls

# ---------- Databricks (free CE or paid) -----------------------------
# Databricks Community Edition at https://community.cloud.databricks.com
# is free forever (restricted features but enough for notebook work).
# DATABRICKS_HOST=https://community.cloud.databricks.com
# DATABRICKS_TOKEN=dapi...

# ---------- Microsoft Fabric (60-day trial) --------------------------
# Fabric workspaces require sign-in; the committed Fabric artefacts
# (notebooks, pipeline JSON, semantic model TMDL) are reviewable even
# without a workspace.
# FABRIC_WORKSPACE_ID=...
# FABRIC_LAKEHOUSE_ID=...

# ---------- Project knobs --------------------------------------------
# Local DuckDB warehouse for Fabric Warehouse / Direct Lake stand-in.
# CLAIMS_DUCKDB_PATH=./warehouse/claims.duckdb
# CLAIMS_LAKEHOUSE_ROOT=./lakehouse
